{
  "baseline_version": "v1.1.0",
  "frozen_at_utc": "2026-05-24T15:02:10.605452+00:00",
  "summary": "First reproducible baseline of the TCGA-GBM nerve-cell pipeline.\nPipeline: GDC loom \u2192 QC \u2192 scVI integration \u2192 CNV-based malignancy labelling \u2192\nnerve-cell subset (re-clustered on X_scVI, 24 Leiden clusters) \u2192\nDE markers (Wilcoxon) \u2192 offline GSEA (gseapy.prerank vs MSigDB C5 GO BP+MF, v2024.1.Hs) \u2192\ncluster annotations / clinical association / tumor\u2013nerve LIANA interactions /\ninteractive marimo enrichment explorer.\nBatch-correction QC: 18 / 24 clusters PASS (median dominant-sample fraction 0.313;\nmedian normalised entropy 0.722 of 4.087 bits).\n\nv1.1.0 deltas (2026-05-24, post failing-cluster diagnosis):\n- cl21 dropped from downstream _with_qc.csv tables via\n  nerve_cells.batch_qc.exclude_clusters (dissociation artifact:\n  stress-marker dominant \u2014 MT-RNR2/1, RPL41, B2M, FTH1; see\n  markdowns/failing_cluster_diagnosis.md).\n- Ependymal added as 5th cell-type label (FOXJ1/RFX3/DNAH7-9-11/\n  CFAP54/PIFO/RSPH1 marker set) and to nerve_cells.cell_types so\n  cells pass the nerve_cell_subset filter. After re-clustering with\n  the +5,713 ependymal cells, three ependymal-dominant clusters\n  emerged: cl11 (72% ependymal, 2,585 cells), cl15 (89%, 1,854 cells),\n  and cl19 (83%, 1,020 cells; clean motile-cilia signature CFAP54/\n  DNAH7/DNAH9). cl11 and cl15 were not predicted by the cut doc;\n  they represent biologically distinct ependymal subpopulations.\n- scANVI v2 retrained on 5 labels (was 4 + Unknown): astrocyte 22,600\n  / neuron 20,538 / ependymal 14,545 / oligodendrocyte 14,380 /\n  opc 13,219 + Unknown 21,321. Classifier accuracy 0.85 (was 0.84).\n- notebooks/02_nerve_enrichment_explorer.py: added 'ependymal' theme\n  regex (CILIUM/CILIARY/AXONEMAL/DYNEIN/EPENDYM) to surface cl11/15/19\n  ciliary GSEA hits in the theme roll-up.\n- v1.0.0 baseline (provenance/baseline_v1.0.0.json) remains frozen\n  and citable.\n",
